Ladybird decodes all of a tab’s SVG images in one page, so a frame
request has to say which image’s document it’s for. The other engines
give each SVG image a page of its own, so a frame request can only reach
that image: Blink’s SVGImage creates an IsolatedSVGDocumentHost for each
image, WebKit’s SVGImage::dataChanged() creates its own Page, and
Gecko’s VectorImage holds its own SVGDocumentWrapper.
